Post-AGI Alpha Hunt =E2=80=94 10 Sep 2026 Executive view

This run produced three genuinely new primitives rather than another list
of AI hardware suppliers:

   1. *Fab activation latency* =E2=80=94 owning a lithography/tool slot is
   economically useless until the physical site, cleanroom and utilities ar=
e
   ready.
   2. *World-state consistency infrastructure* =E2=80=94 increasingly capab=
le
   agents need an authoritative, continuously updated representation of wha=
t
   actually exists in the physical world.
   3. *Failure-history / negative-data moats* =E2=80=94 autonomous scientis=
ts
   explicitly improve by remembering unsuccessful directions; data that hum=
ans
   historically discard can become the most defensible training asset.

The highest-alpha public-company rabbit holes are *Takasago Thermal
Engineering (1969.T)* and *VusionGroup (VU.PA <http://VU.PA>)*. The most
important non-stock research branch is the *humanoid fail-passive gap*,
because it identifies a new safety-hardware category rather than merely
more certification spending.
1. FAB ACTIVATION LATENCY =E2=80=94 9.4/10 Thesis

The semiconductor bottleneck is migrating from *tool availability* toward *=
the
ability to turn purchased tools into qualified production capacity*.

ASML=E2=80=99s FY2026 guidance explicitly says customer readiness to receiv=
e
systems =E2=80=94 including fab completion and cleanroom availability =E2=
=80=94 is a major
determinant of the wide revenue range. That is unusually direct evidence
that the scarce object is becoming *activated cleanroom capacity*, not just
equipment.

Micron=E2=80=99s Hiroshima expansion illustrates the time mismatch: a =C2=
=A51.5tn
AI-memory project is adding ~28,000 m=C2=B2 of cleanroom, yet equipment mov=
e-in
is not scheduled until H2 2028. Intelligence/design cycles can compress
dramatically; certified physical manufacturing space cannot.
Candidate exposure: Takasago Thermal Engineering (1969.T)

Japanese HVAC / environmental-engineering specialist with direct relevance
to high-spec industrial facilities. FY ended Mar-2026 revenue rose 11.1% to
=C2=A5423.9bn while operating profit jumped 47.3%; orders exceeded =C2=A546=
0bn.
Market cap is roughly =C2=A50.57=E2=80=930.64tn depending source/date.

This is not a pure semiconductor name, which is precisely why it is
interesting: if high-spec cleanroom/environmental engineering becomes the
gating layer, earnings can inflect before the narrative catches up.
New kernel variable

activation_latency =3D time(tool_committed -> qualified_output)

And:

stranded_tool_risk =3D committed_equipment_value =C3=97 probability(site_no=
t_ready)
Caveat

The earnings surge is already visible, and Japan construction
inflation/labor constraints can compress margins. Exposure is diversified
rather than pure-play.
Falsifier

If fab/cleanroom completion stays consistently ahead of WFE deliveries and
ASML/customer commentary stops citing site readiness as a delivery
constraint, downgrade the thesis.

Evidence: ASML FY2026 commentary; Micron Hiroshima groundbreaking and
cleanroom timetable; Takasago FY2026 results.
2. WORLD-STATE CONSISTENCY INFRASTRUCTURE =E2=80=94 9.2/10 Thesis

Post-AGI agents can reason over digital information nearly instantly, but
they cannot act correctly if the digital representation of reality is stale=
.

That creates a new scarce commodity:

*authoritative physical state.*

Examples: what product is physically on a shelf, its actual price, which
asset revision is installed, whether a machine is available, whether a
component has moved, whether inventory exists, whether an instrument is
calibrated.

The investment implication is subtle: the value can accrue not to the agent
but to the *sensor/identity/update layer that continuously reconciles
digital world models with atoms*.
Candidate exposure: VusionGroup (VU.PA)

VusionCloud now manages *>500 million connected electronic shelf labels*,
versus ~220m one year earlier. H1 2026 adjusted revenue grew 29%
organically; recurring value-added-services revenue grew 73%, with
annualized recurring VAS revenue up 83%.

This network is interesting beyond electronic price tags. It is effectively
a giant installed mesh linking physical retail locations to cloud state. In
an agentic-commerce world, machine-readable, continuously synchronized
shelf state becomes much more valuable.

Current valuation screens are surprisingly moderate after the selloff:
roughly =E2=82=AC2bn market cap and ~17x 2026 forward earnings / ~11x 2027
estimates depending source.
Why this is different from ordinary IoT

IoT measures things. *World-state consistency infrastructure settles
disagreements between the digital model and physical reality.*

Kernel edge:

digital_claim --verified_by--> physical_state

New feature:

state_decay_rate =3D probability(digital representation becomes wrong per
unit time)

The faster the physical environment changes, the more valuable low-latency
synchronization becomes.
Caveats

H1 order intake was down 22% YoY despite improving sequentially. ESLs also
face political/regulatory backlash around dynamic pricing; U.S. state
restrictions could slow deployments.
Falsifier

If retailers obtain equivalent real-time state cheaply from
cameras/robots/computer vision without needing dense tagged infrastructure,
Vusion-style endpoint density loses strategic value.
3. NEGATIVE-DATA MOATS =E2=80=94 9.0/10 conceptual alpha Fresh evidence

The March 2026 *EvoScientist* paper does something economically important:
its persistent memories explicitly record *unsuccessful research directions=
*
so future agents avoid repeating failed experiments. The authors report
improved idea quality and code-execution success versus seven
open/commercial AI-scientist systems.

This supports a stronger formulation of our negative-data thesis:

As model intelligence commoditizes, proprietary records of what *doesn=E2=
=80=99t
work under specific real conditions* become disproportionately valuable.

Humans systematically discard this information because journals reward
successful results. Autonomous systems do the opposite: failed trajectories
reduce future search cost.
New metric

negative_information_value =3D avoided_future_experiment_cost =C3=97
probability(agent_would_repeat_failure)

And:

failure_capture_ratio =3D recorded_failed_trials / actual_failed_trials

A company with mediocre positive-data IP but near-complete failure
histories may possess a better AI-era moat than a company with a clean
publication corpus.
Tradable exposure

No convincing pure-play public exposure yet. Avoid forcing one. The better
alpha hunt is to identify industries where experiments are expensive and
failure logs remain proprietary: semiconductor process recipes, specialty
chemicals, aerospace qualification, biologics process development, battery
formation, industrial catalysts.
Falsifier

If frontier models infer unsuccessful regions accurately enough from
positive observations/physics that explicit failure histories provide
little incremental improvement, the moat collapses.
4. HUMANOID FAIL-PASSIVE GAP =E2=80=94 8.9/10

This is a material refinement of the earlier certification-bandwidth thesis=
.

An August 2026 paper argues industrial humanoids have a structural safety
problem: conventional machine safety assumes that removing power moves
equipment toward a safe state. For a balancing biped, removing power can *c=
ause
an uncontrolled fall*.

That means classical safety components do not cleanly transfer. The paper
can certify the external safety chain but localizes the unresolved problem
to the robot-side reaction chain / balancing controller.
Investment implication

Humanoid deployment may create an entirely new hardware stack:

   - safety-rated active stabilization
   - redundant actuation/power paths
   - safety-rated compute
   - fail-operational motor control
   - controlled-energy braking
   - independent balance sensing
   - validated low-latency safety networking

The alpha is therefore not just T=C3=9CV/SGS certification. It is *new safe=
ty
BOM per robot*.
Candidate exposure

Novanta (NOVT) is worth monitoring because it sells precision
motion/control components and its robotics/automation bookings have been
strong, but valuation is already demanding (~36=E2=80=9339x forward earning=
s; ~29x
EV/EBITDA on current screens). Siemens/ABB provide less convex but broader
safety-control exposure.
Falsifier

If mechanical architectures evolve so humanoids naturally collapse into
passive safe states, or regulators accept software-only safety cases
without redundant hardware, the incremental safety BOM is much smaller.
5. SIMULATION SUCCESS CREATES A REALITY-CALIBRATION TAX =E2=80=94 8.6/10

Recent work on interactive robot world models reports policies trained on
generated interactions performing comparably to policies trained with
equivalent real-world data, with simulation and real-world performance
strongly correlated.

At first glance this destroys experimental scarcity.

The second-order implication is more interesting:

*cheap synthetic experience increases the marginal value of the
comparatively tiny stream of real-world observations needed to verify that
the simulator remains correct.*

As simulation volume approaches infinity:

value(real calibration sample) =E2=86=91

especially around rare failures, deformable materials, wear, contamination,
human interaction and novel environments.

This suggests a barbell:

   - abundant synthetic training data becomes cheap;
   - sparse, high-integrity physical edge-case data becomes expensive.

That links back to Samsara/Vusion-style physical telemetry, autonomous-lab
traces, industrial condition monitoring and robot fleet data.
Falsifier

If foundation world models generalize across physical distribution shifts
with negligible ongoing real-world calibration, the reality-calibration tax
falls sharply.
Ranking
Rank New rabbit hole Expected alpha Best current exposure
1 Fab activation latency / cleanroom readiness *9.4* Takasago Thermal 1969.=
T
2 World-state consistency infrastructure *9.2* VusionGroup VU.PA
3 Negative-data moats *9.0* No clean pure-play yet
4 Humanoid fail-passive safety stack *8.9* NOVT watchlist; Siemens/ABB
diluted
5 Reality-calibration tax after world-model scaling *8.6* telemetry /
sensor layer Kernel additions

activation_latency

stranded_tool_risk

state_decay_rate

world_state_reconciliation_frequency

failure_capture_ratio

negative_information_value

active_safety_content_per_robot

reality_calibration_ratio =3D real observations / synthetic observations

The most promising next decomposition is *world-state consistency*: locate
obscure public companies that provide identity, serialization,
localization, version/revision tracking, machine-readable shelf/inventory
state, and as-built/as-maintained truth for physical assets. That is likely
to cut across retail, factories, robotics, construction, defense and
autonomous labs rather than depend on one AGI implementation.

